{
  "title": "Pangea™ Extra Articular Distal Humerus Plate",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/implants/423200/pangea-tm--extra-articular-distal-humerus-plate",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 9 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Related Implants",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea™ series contains 3 humerus plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Proximal Humerus**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Proximal Humerus Posterior**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Extra Articular Distal Humerus (this topic)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pangea Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Variable Angle Locking Technology**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Pangea’s variable angle locking technology uses a CoCr locking screw, which is harder than the Ti6Al4V ELI plate, allowing for the screwhead’s threads to form a definitive plate-screw interface in the plate's locking hole by engaging the softer, Ti6Al4V material.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423200/images/a548cbed-f3ba-4d20-b53e-70f8a8baa299_screenshot_2025-01-08_at_11.14.04_am.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "This technology allows the user to aim and lock the screw into the plate within a true 30° cone of the predetermined hole trajectory. The variable angle drill guide provided with the system offers guidance with respect to the limit of the 30° cone. The locking mechanism remains functional for up to three attempts at locking screw insertion.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Circular holes that accommodate screws are universal; accepting non-locking screws and locking screws within a 30° cone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Increased Proximal Plate Thickness**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed to provide robust humerus shaft fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**2.0mm Proximal K-Wire Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423200/images/560f45e2-4af6-4338-8bb7-f71a1a03f8db_screenshot_2025-01-08_at_11.13.41_am.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed to provide temporary fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Rounded and Tapered End**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed to allow for smooth insertion under the soft tissue",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Waisted Scalloped Shape**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Hybrid LC Holes (locking/compression)**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Hybrid LC Holes allow for either active compression with the use of a non-locking screw in the compression section of the hole or variable angle locking with the use of a locking screw in the universal section of the hole. If locking is not desired, the universal section of the hole also accepts non-locking screws. Each Hybrid LC Hole is designed to provide up to 2mm of compression.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Distal 2.0mm K-Wire Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Points into the center of the capitellum to ensure correct plate placement and reduce the potential for impingement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423200/images/560f45e2-4af6-4338-8bb7-f71a1a03f8db_screenshot_2025-01-08_at_11.13.41_am.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Placement",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The distal portion of the plate should be placed lateral to the trochlea and the olecranon fossa on the posterior aspect of the distal humerus",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Fixed angle drill sleeve may be used as a handle for control of plate placement and positioning. 1",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fit",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Plate was designed using SOMA analytics to improve anatomic fit and reduce the potential for impingement with the radial head in full extension. 2",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Plate extends further distally than competitive systems such as Synthes and Skeletal Dynamics, further increasing the distal fixation by increasing the working length of the plate. 2",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technical specifications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Plate Lengths: 4-14 holes (130-300mm)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Thickness: 4.2mm proximally, 2.0mm distally",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Left and right anatomic plate options",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Drill bits: Ø2.5mm x 135mm (542020) Ø2.5mm x 215mm (542021)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea Humerus Plating System is indicated for the internal fixation and stabilization of humerus bone fractures and osteotomies in normal and osteopenic bone, including:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Diaphyseal, metaphyseal, epiphyseal, extra- and intra-articular fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Non-unions, malunions, and deformities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Periprosthetic fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Approaches",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Surgeons may use a standard posterior paratriceptial approach to the distal 1/3 of the humerus.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Depending on the fracture pattern, a surgeon may use a triceps splitting approach.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
